urlview/1e: Apply patch (portability): Provide an overflow-checked `reallocarray()` in the header shared by the C
and the C++ units.  The OHOS libc image ships neither a declaration nor a
symbol for it (`llvm-nm -D --defined-only <sysroot>/lib/aarch64-linux-ohos/libc.so
| grep -c reallocarray` -> 0, and `-D_GNU_SOURCE` still leaves the call
undeclared), so urlview.c and the BUMPCHAR()/init grow paths in enter.cpp
cannot build or link as shipped.

urlview/1e: Apply patch (portability): Let the build opt out of gettext through `-DURLVIEW_NO_GETTEXT` and make the
two probes in urlview.c agree by a single `UV_USE_GETTEXT` flag.  The OHOS
sysroot has a `<libintl.h>` that is a macro-only stub: it passes upstream's
`__has_include(<libintl.h>)` probe, declares neither `gettext()` nor
`bindtextdomain()`, and there is no libintl in the sysroot to link against.
Opting out lands on upstream's own identity fallback (`gettext(s) (s)`),
which is the intended no-gettext configuration and matches the fact that no
catalogue is installed by this recipe either.

